{"abstract":[{"text":"Add MarkdownKit to a project, parse a Markdown string into a syntax tree and find out what it contains.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GettingStarted"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"MarkdownKit"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Getting Started"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"MarkdownKit parses Markdown text into an abstract syntax tree, which you can inspect, transform, and convert into HTML, plain text, text for ANSI terminals, or an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSAttributedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This article shows how to add the framework to a project and how to parse a document.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Add-MarkdownKit-to-your-project","level":3,"text":"Add MarkdownKit to your project","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"MarkdownKit is distributed as a Swift package. Add it to the dependencies of your ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and to the target that uses it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["dependencies: [","  .package(url: \"https://github.com/objecthub/swift-markdownkit.git\", from: \"2.1.0\")","],","targets: [","  .target(name: \"MyApp\", dependencies: [","    .product(name: \"MarkdownKit\", package: \"swift-markdownkit\")","  ])","]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In Xcode, choose File > Add Package Dependencies and enter the URL of the repository. The framework is compiled in Swift 6 language mode; clients can use any language mode.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Parse-a-document","level":3,"text":"Parse a document","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" provides a simple API for parsing Markdown in a string. The parser returns an abstract syntax tree representing the Markdown structure in the string:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import MarkdownKit","","let markdown = MarkdownParser.standard.parse(\"\"\"","                 # Header","                 ## Sub-header","                 And this is a **paragraph**.","                 \"\"\")","print(markdown)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Executing this code prints the following data structure of type ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["document(heading(1, text(\"Header\")),","         heading(2, text(\"Sub-header\")),","         paragraph(text(\"And this is a \"),","                   strong(text(\"paragraph\")),","                   text(\".\")))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is a recursively defined enumeration of cases with associated values (also called an ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"algebraic datatype","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"). Case ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block/document(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" refers to the root of a document. It contains a sequence of blocks. In the example above, two different types of blocks appear within the document: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block/heading(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block/paragraph(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"heading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" case consists of a heading level (as its first argument) and heading text (as the second argument). A ","type":"text"},{"code":"paragraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" case simply consists of text.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Text is represented using the struct ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which is effectively a sequence of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TextFragment","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" values. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TextFragment","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is yet another recursively defined enumeration with associated values. The example above shows two different ","type":"text"},{"code":"TextFragment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cases in action: ","type":"text"},{"code":"text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"strong","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Case ","type":"text"},{"code":"text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" represents plain strings. Case ","type":"text"},{"code":"strong","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" contains a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" object, i.e. it encapsulates a sequence of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TextFragment","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" values which are “marked up strongly”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Choose-what-to-do-next","level":3,"text":"Choose what to do next","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To parse tables, definition lists, underlined or struck-through text and task lists, pick the right parser: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ChoosingAParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To find things in a document or to change it, walk the syntax tree: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ProcessingMarkdown","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To turn a document into HTML, text or attributed strings: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To show a document in a SwiftUI view: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DisplayingMarkdownWithSwiftUI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To add your own syntax: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ExtendingTheParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Know-the-limits","level":3,"text":"Know the limits","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The parser passes all 652 examples of the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". The test suite compares the generated HTML with the reference HTML of the specification, ignoring differences that do not change how browsers render the output: whitespace outside of code, ","type":"text"},{"code":"&quot;","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" vs. ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"<ol start=\"1\">","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" vs. ","type":"text"},{"code":"<ol>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and percent-encoding of URLs (MarkdownKit does not encode URLs).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"There are a number of limitations:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Extensions of GitHub Flavored Markdown other than tables, strikethrough and task lists (supported by ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") are not supported: extended autolinks and footnotes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The block parser keeps trailing spaces and backslashes at the end of the lines of a paragraph; whether a line ending is a hard line break is only decided by the inline parser (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/EscapeTransformer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"), because it depends on the inline markup (e.g. code spans). If you only parse the block structure (","type":"text"},{"code":"blockOnly: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), hard line breaks are not recognized.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Check-the-platform-requirements","level":3,"text":"Check the platform requirements","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"MarkdownKit supports Apple platforms only: macOS 11, iOS 15, tvOS 15 and watchOS 8 or later. Linux and other non-Apple platforms are not supported.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Syntax highlighting relies on JavaScriptCore and is not available on watchOS.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mermaid diagrams rely on WebKit and are only available on macOS and iOS.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The SwiftUI view ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is available on macOS 14 and iOS 17 or later.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The command-line tools are only functional on macOS.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Building the framework requires Xcode 16 or later (it is developed with Xcode 26) and a Swift 6 toolchain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Parse, process and display text in Markdown format.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"MarkdownKit","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator":{"abstract":[{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides functionality for converting Markdown blocks into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSAttributedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects that are used in macOS and iOS for displaying rich text.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The implementation is extensible allowing subclasses of ","type":"text"},{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"override how individual Markdown structures are converted into attributed strings.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block":{"abstract":[{"text":"Enumeration of Markdown blocks. This enumeration defines the block structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"i.e. the abstract syntax, of Markdown supported by MarkdownKit. The structure of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inline text is defined by the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" struct.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Block"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Block"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Block","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/block"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block/document(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"The root of a document: the sequence of its top-level blocks.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"document"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit6Blocksa","text":"Blocks"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block/document(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"Block.document(_:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/block/document(_:)"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block/heading(_:_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"A heading. The first parameter is the heading level, from 1 (the most important heading)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to 6. The second parameter is the text of the heading.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"heading"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit4TextV","text":"Text"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block/heading(_:_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"Block.heading(_:_:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/block/heading(_:_:)"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block/paragraph(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"A paragraph containing inline text.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"paragraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit4TextV","text":"Text"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block/paragraph(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"Block.paragraph(_:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/block/paragraph(_:)"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ChoosingAParser":{"abstract":[{"text":"Pick the parser class that supports the Markdown syntax your documents use.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ChoosingAParser","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Choosing a Parser","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/choosingaparser"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DisplayingMarkdownWithSwiftUI":{"abstract":[{"text":"Show a Markdown document in a SwiftUI view, and adapt it to light and dark mode.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DisplayingMarkdownWithSwiftUI","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Displaying Markdown with SwiftUI","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/displayingmarkdownwithswiftui"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/EscapeTransformer":{"abstract":[{"text":"An inline transformer which removes backslash escapes. It also determines which line endings","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are hard line breaks (a backslash or at least two spaces at the end of a line) and removes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trailing white space in front of other line endings.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EscapeTransformer"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/EscapeTransformer","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EscapeTransformer"}],"role":"symbol","title":"EscapeTransformer","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/escapetransformer"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ExtendingTheParser":{"abstract":[{"text":"Add your own inline markup to the Markdown syntax that MarkdownKit supports.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ExtendingTheParser","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Extending the Parser","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/extendingtheparser"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser":{"abstract":[{"code":"FullMarkdownParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects are used to parse Markdown text represented as a string using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"all features of MarkdownKit: the syntax of the CommonMark specification and all extensions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that MarkdownKit implements.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FullMarkdownParser"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FullMarkdownParser"}],"role":"symbol","title":"FullMarkdownParser","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/fullmarkdownparser"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput":{"abstract":[{"text":"Convert a parsed Markdown document into HTML, attributed strings, plain text or text for ANSI terminals.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Generating Output","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/generatingoutput"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser":{"abstract":[{"code":"MarkdownParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects are used to parse Markdown text represented as a string.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"MarkdownParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" object itself defines the configuration of the parser. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stateless in the sense that it can be used for parsing many input strings. This is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"done via the ","type":"text"},{"code":"parse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function. ","type":"text"},{"code":"parse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns an abstract syntax tree representing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the Markdown text for the given input string.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MarkdownParser"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownParser","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MarkdownParser"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MarkdownParser","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/markdownparser"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText":{"abstract":[{"text":"A SwiftUI view that displays a Markdown document as formatted text. The view converts the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document into an attributed string with an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", using different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generators for light and dark mode, and shows the result in a read-only text view whose text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be selected. The view scrolls vertically.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MarkdownText"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MarkdownText"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MarkdownText","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/markdowntext"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MigrationGuide":{"abstract":[{"text":"Find out what to change in your code when you update MarkdownKit.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MigrationGuide","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Migrating to Newer Versions","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/migrationguide"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ProcessingMarkdown":{"abstract":[{"text":"Walk the abstract syntax tree of a parsed document to extract information or to transform it.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/ProcessingMarkdown","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Processing Markdown","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/processingmarkdown"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Recipes":{"abstract":[{"text":"Solve common tasks with a few lines of MarkdownKit.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Recipes","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Recipes","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/recipes"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text":{"abstract":[{"text":"Struct ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is used to represent inline text. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct consists of a sequence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"TextFragment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Text","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/text"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TextFragment":{"abstract":[{"text":"In MarkdownKit, text with markup is represented as a sequence of ","type":"text"},{"code":"TextFragment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each ","type":"text"},{"code":"TextFragment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enumeration variant represents one form of inline markup. Since","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"markup can be arbitrarily nested, this is a recursive data structure (via struct ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextFragment"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/TextFragment","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextFragment"}],"role":"symbol","title":"TextFragment","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/textfragment"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingMarkdownKitConcurrently":{"abstract":[{"text":"Parse and generate on background threads and tasks, and know what to restate in subclasses.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingMarkdownKitConcurrently","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Using MarkdownKit Concurrently","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/usingmarkdownkitconcurrently"},"https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/":{"identifier":"https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/","title":"CommonMark 0.31.2 specification","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"CommonMark 0.31.2 specification","type":"text"}],"type":"link","url":"https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/"}},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Recipes","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/UsingMarkdownKitConcurrently","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MigrationGuide"],"title":"Essentials"}],"variants":[{"paths":["/documentation/markdownkit/gettingstarted"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}]}